02\\game\\index.html:143-153` checks the reversal against `dir`, while `:88-91` applies `nextDir` on a tick and prepends the new head; `:101-112` detects the resulting body collision; ticks are scheduled every 120 ms at `:164`. - **Recommendation:** Validate a new turn against the pending direction (`nextDir`) as well as the current direction so consecutive inputs cannot queue an immediate reversal. ### Rough edges and suggestions - **Controls are not labeled on the page.** The visible markup includes the game title, score, canvas, and game-over restart button, while the only controls handled in source are arrow keys (`...\\index.html:42-50`, `:143-153`). A small “Use arrow keys to move” hint could help a first-time player discover the controls. Since I could not open the page, this is based on the markup, not a visual runtime observation. ### Review limits I could not exercise startup, gameplay, game-over, restart, or browser/runtime errors in a live browser. No browser-based claims are made; the confirmed finding is established by tracing the input and tick logic in the source. </agent-message>","permission_mode":"auto","session_id":"21c5e7de-28af-4b8a-aa9b-2e9b777124fc"}
